From 9076c2cf905ffe49d1fc328a3db7314a9dfb1cb5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 22:11:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] shared: make SystemUI's androidx.core.animation follow the
 system scale

androidx.core.animation keeps its own static duration scale at 1.0 and
only has a package-private setter, so SystemUI animations built on it
(status bar event chips, keyguard status bar fade, notification
drag-expand, remote input, lockscreen shortcut shake) ran full length with
animations off. The library is a prebuilt, so add a small bridge class in
its package inside SystemUI that copies the platform animator duration
scale at startup and on every change.

Change-Id: Ifeecd3a009feaa7270bdfecda1072eb057d89b3d
---
 .../PlatformDurationScaleBridge.java          | 41 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../impl/SystemUIApplicationImpl.java         |  2 +
 2 files changed, 43 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 packages/SystemUI/src/androidx/core/animation/PlatformDurationScaleBridge.java

diff --git a/packages/SystemUI/src/androidx/core/animation/PlatformDurationScaleBridge.java b/packages/SystemUI/src/androidx/core/animation/PlatformDurationScaleBridge.java
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..800d3acbc
--- /dev/null
+++ b/packages/SystemUI/src/androidx/core/animation/PlatformDurationScaleBridge.java
@@ -0,0 +1,41 @@
